U-Boot rockusb: report the RV1103B / RV1106B chip id ("110E") so upgrade_tool can flash in Loader mode

Proposal for build-ai-ego/rockchip-platforms (branch rv1106-bg2-main), found on 2026-10-13 by the
first real run of BuildAI Serial Utility's Firmware tab on the Node board 0225ce3c8d8d6e44:

  `adb reboot loader` brings the board into U-Boot's rockusb (Mode=Loader, PID 0x110E) as designed,
  but the Windows upgrade_tool.exe v2.37 stops `UF update.img` with

      Test Device Success
      Check Chip Start
      Check Chip Fail
      Note:read chip info by rkdevtool and use new chip to create firmware

  and its log says `CheckChip-->Chip is not match,firmware(0x31313045),device(0x0)`:
  `upgrade_tool RCI` reads `Chip Info: 0 0 0 0 ...` from the loader. The cause is in
  sysdrv/source/uboot/u-boot/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/chip_info.c: rockchip_rockusb_get_chip_info()
  has a rockusb fixup for RV1106 (0x31313036 = "1106") and RV1126 but none for CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_RV1103B
  (the rv1106b_defconfig family), so the 16 bytes stay zero. The firmware package carries the
  chip tag "110E" (0x31313045), which the tool compares with the device's word.

  Nothing was written to the board; `upgrade_tool RD` brought it back to its firmware each time.

The change (one case in the rockusb fixup):

--- a/sysdrv/source/uboot/u-boot/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/chip_info.c
+++ b/sysdrv/source/uboot/u-boot/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/chip_info.c
@@ int rockchip_rockusb_get_chip_info(unsigned int chip_info[])
 #elif defined(CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_RV1126)
 		chip_info[0] = 0x31313236;
 #elif defined(CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_RV1106)
 		chip_info[0] = 0x31313036;
+#elif defined(CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_RV1103B)
+		/* "110E": RV1103B / RV1106B, the chip tag update.img carries (SocToolKit's magic
+		 * table maps both to 110E), so upgrade_tool's Check Chip passes in Loader mode. */
+		chip_info[0] = 0x31313045;
 #endif

After rebuilding U-Boot (and flashing that build once by the way that works today: the Linux
usb_update.sh, the MASKROM button, or the Rockchip GUI tool), `upgrade_tool.exe UF` from the Firmware
tab's Pull & Flash passes Check Chip on this board. The Firmware tab itself needs no change for it:
its flow is the one of tools/usb_update.sh and stops, as seen, at the tool's own verdict.
